    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green.\n\nDone. The GOLD tier rule is implemented with minimal structural impact \u2014 three files touched, no method grown, no change to any large class:\n\n1. **`OwnerHouseholdPolicy.java`** \u2014 one line: every created owner now gets its deterministic `householdId` (previously only the second-and-later member of a shared household did), so all members of a household share the same id. Duplicate-rejection behavior is unchanged.\n\n2. **`OwnerHouseholdTierPostProcessor.java`** (new, tiny cohesive unit) \u2014 a MapStruct `@AfterMapping` component that counts owners sharing the owner's `householdId` and upgrades `membershipTier` to `GOLD` when there are 3 or more.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one annotation edit adding the post-processor to `uses`, so MapStruct invokes it after the existing BRONZE/SILVER expression.\n\nThe GOLD check overrides the BRONZE/SILVER result (GOLD takes precedence); when the household has fewer than 3 members the existing rules stand. Because the tier is derived at read time from the persisted `householdId`, it works across separate transactions and on every configured database with no schema or seed-data changes.",
